# DTF tier manifest: openscap-evaluates-image-rootfs
#   (artifact-keeper#6000, fixed on main for 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + scanners.openscap (the OpenSCAP wrapper sidecar,
# OPENSCAP_IMAGE, sharing the backend's scan workspace read-only, as in the
# stock compose file). LOCAL-ONLY: the base layer of the test images is a
# `docker export` of the running sidecar (a UBI 9 system), filtered to /etc,
# /usr/lib/os-release and the rpmdb, so nothing is pulled.
#
# THE BUG
# #6000  Every OpenSCAP scan evaluated the OpenSCAP sidecar's own filesystem.
#        The backend wrote the artifact's raw bytes (for an image, the
#        manifest JSON) into the workspace as one file; the wrapper found no
#        etc/ there, so oscap's probes ran against the sidecar's `/`, and the
#        findings were the same whatever the artifact. RPM and DEB packages
#        were "scanned" the same way. The default profile
#        (content_profile_standard) is in no shipped datastream and was
#        silently replaced by anssi_bp28_enhanced.
#        Fixed: the backend unpacks the image's layers into a root filesystem
#        and the wrapper evaluates it with OSCAP_PROBE_ROOT; packages and
#        images no shipped datastream describes are not_applicable; the
#        default is CIS Level 1 - Server and an unknown profile is an error.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) every image: three test images push (two layers each for RHEL,
#     one for Debian); the clean RHEL 9 image gets a terminal openscap row
#     without file_permissions_etc_shadow or groups_no_zero_gid_except_root.
#   (FIX) #6000, RED on main before the fix (and 1.11.x), GREEN after it:
#     * the noncompliant image (its top layer sets /etc/shadow 0644 and adds a
#       second GID-0 group) is completed WITH both findings, and its findings
#       differ from the clean image's (pre-fix: both images get the sidecar's
#       identical findings, neither rule among them);
#     * an image whose os-release is Debian 12 is not_applicable and the
#       reason names it (pre-fix: completed);
#     * an .rpm uploaded to a generic repository is not_applicable (pre-fix:
#       completed with the sidecar's findings).
#
# GREEN needs the fixed backend AND the fixed OpenSCAP image together
# (OPENSCAP_IMAGE=<fixed>): the fixed backend refuses a pre-fix wrapper's
# answer (it carries no scan status) and fails those scans.
#
# NOT GATED: the default/unknown-profile handling (no profile is visible in
# scan_results; the backend and wrapper unit tests cover it), ownership-rule
# exclusion, and the Docker-runtime path where user namespaces are blocked
# (this profile runs the sidecar seccomp=unconfined; see the profile).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: registry pushes and scan polls back to back.
COVERS="6000"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem scanners.openscap"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
